{"seq":14,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-acl-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-acl-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-03T15:41:57.516Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"ab96eddf098898a6ea03e4a190b8ec3cd127637a9adff7b62dd85a1b55353347","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files (the North and Central digests and cheat sheets). I found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. There's a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't say when this one was raised.\n\nSome things I left out:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in the Central handoff digest, but they belong to Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n• Moss's 9/14 pipeline digest and 3/23 renewal note mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers.\n• Quarendon Freightways is a different company and not one of our customers, so I didn't include anything about it."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
